WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.660
Twenty-five years after
roaring into theaters,

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:06.270
"The Lion King" is back,

00:00:06.270 --> 00:00:10.410
this time with a more realistic look.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.390
But is the remake really
more true-to-nature

00:00:13.390 --> 00:00:14.423
than the original?

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:19.840
To be fair to Disney,

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:23.440
they did fix some mistakes
from the original version.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.930
Take Rafiki.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.570
In one scene in the 1994 film,

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:31.620
he and Simba argue about
which one of them is a baboon.

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:34.380
It means you're a baboon, and I'm not.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.900
NARRATOR: Clearly,
Simba is not a baboon...

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.870
but neither is Rafiki.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:43.370
He's a different kind of
monkey altogether, a mandrill.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:47.360
And what's more, Rafiki has a long tail,

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:51.380
yet in real life, mandrills
are nearly tailless.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:54.780
Luckily, Disney fixes this
problem in the remake,

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.780
so now Rafiki looks like the
mandrill he's meant to be.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.580
But unfortunately,

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:05.210
Disney didn't get the
mandrills' behavior quite right.

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:07.770
See how they're swinging
through the trees?

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:09.350
Yeah.

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.120
Mandrills don't really do that.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.010
They spend most of their
time on the ground,

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:17.590
and when they do take to the trees,

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.800
they walk across the
branches on all fours.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.950
This swinging behavior
is actually more similar

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.870
to how a gibbon moves.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.140
But enough about mandrills.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:31.500
What about the lions of "The Lion King"?

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.863
Well, there are a few problems there, too.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.979
Take the iconic lion roar.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.360
Sounds majestic, right?

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.693
Just like the famous MGM roar.

00:01:49.120 --> 00:01:50.310
Here's the issue.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.570
A lion's roar doesn't sound like that.

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:55.103
This is a roar.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.010
It's not quite as majestic as
what you hear in the movie,

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:02.360
but that sound can still travel

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.610
up to 8 kilometers away.

00:02:08.107 --> 00:02:12.540
Some of the lions' behavior is also off...

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:15.274
and that's not including
talking with ghosts.

00:02:15.274 --> 00:02:16.740
MUFASA: Remember.

00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:20.350
NARRATOR: Watch how Simba
scampers off with his dad.

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:23.690
It's a touching scene, but in real life,

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:27.130
Sarabi would never let
Simba out of her sight.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.150
While lion cubs do play
with their fathers,

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:33.010
their mothers are extremely protective.

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:37.300
And you can't blame them because
if a new male comes to town

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:38.877
and takes over the pride,

00:02:38.877 --> 00:02:41.900
he'll try to kill their young cubs.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.121
Sound familiar?

00:02:43.121 --> 00:02:44.770
That's right.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:47.280
Scar's scheme to usurp Mufasa

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.540
was in line with normal lion behavior,

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:55.090
except his methods were
rather unconventional

00:02:55.940 --> 00:02:59.303
because lions and hyenas
don't work together.

00:02:59.303 --> 00:03:00.730
Ever.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:05.480
In fact, they're major
competitors for food in the wild.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:08.200
So it's hard to believe that a lion

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.240
could convince a hoard of
hyenas to do his dirty work,

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.899
even with a catchy villain song.

00:03:14.899 --> 00:03:17.399
♪ Be prepared ♪

